  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">New Multicultural Identities in Europe (2014), published by Leuven University Press, has been cited 1 time. Beyond that, it has been downloaded 2,334 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">New Multicultural Identities in Europe by Erkan Toğuşlu was published by Leuven University Press in 2014. Conceptually, the work connects to Globalization, Glocalization, Multiculturalism, Sociology and Transnationalism.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 1 citation. Notable citing venues include The British Accounting Review. They come from 2 countries, led by the United Kingdom and Greece.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It has been downloaded 2,334 times via OAPEN. Its subject matter aligns with Reduced inequalities among the Sustainable Development Goals.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\" data-wiki-books=\"verified\">The latest English Wikipedia check verified 1 article–work reference matches. These are references or bibliography entries, which may include other editions of the same work; they do not measure readership.</p>\n",
